## What it is

The Precision Brewer (model BDC450) is Breville's high-end drip machine. It looks like an ordinary coffee maker, but a PID-controlled Thermocoil heater keeps the water temperature steady, and you can change the bloom time and flow rate yourself.

- **Capacity:** 60oz, brewing into a brushed stainless thermal carafe (no hot plate)
- **Presets:** Gold (built around the SCA's Gold Cup standard), Fast, Strong, Over Ice and Cold Brew
- **My Brew:** your own settings for bloom time, flow rate and temperature
- **Baskets:** both a flat-bottom basket and a cone insert, and it works with Breville's pour-over adapter
- **Speed:** a full 12 cups in under 7 minutes on Fast

Breville has since discontinued this model. There's more on its replacement at the end of this review.

## How I use it

This is my go-to coffee maker whenever I need to make a larger amount: when people are over, or when I want coffee for the whole morning. For one cup I'll reach for pour-over, but when it's time for a full pot, this is the one I use.

Most of the time I just use the Gold setting and press start. The thermal carafe keeps the coffee hot without cooking it on a burner, so the last cup tastes nearly as good as the first.

## The good and the bad

The best thing I can say about it is that it's been easy to use and dependable for me for many years. It's never let me down, and I haven't had to think about it beyond descaling now and then.

The extra settings are there if you want to play with them. You don't need them to get a good pot. It's big, though, at almost 16" tall, so measure under your cabinets first.

## Would I buy it again?

Yes. It's the one machine in my kitchen I don't think about anymore, and for a coffee maker, that's the highest praise I can give.

## If you're buying one now

Since the Precision Brewer is discontinued, the closest thing you can buy new is Breville's [Luxe Brewer Thermal](https://www.breville.com/en-us/product/bdc465?sku=BDC465BSS1BNA1) (BDC465, $349.95). I haven't used the Luxe myself, so I can't vouch for it the way I can for mine. On paper it's the same kind of machine: a 60oz thermal carafe, brewing to the SCA Golden Cup standard, with adjustable bloom, flow rate and temperature.

It also adds a few things mine doesn't have:

- a water filter built into a removable tank
- a delayed start, up to 24 hours ahead
- a carafe Breville says keeps coffee above 150°F for up to 4 hours

In exchange, it trades my machine's Fast, Strong and Over Ice presets for a simpler One Touch and Custom Brew setup.
